course: dictionary
lesson: 1361
title: Cannon: a gun, a crash, and a spray
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cannon is one word with three meanings, so the words around it tell you which one you need. The first meaning is a big, heavy gun that fires metal balls or shells. In «The cannon they are shooting», the word shooting is a clue that the cannon is a weapon.
explain: The verb meaning is different. To cannon into someone is to crash into them hard while moving fast. If «Amir cannoned into Sam in the corridor», he did not fire anything. He ran into Sam with a bump. Water cannon is a third use: a machine that sprays very strong jets of water.
explain: Always check by swapping in your meaning. Does «the big gun they are shooting» still make sense? Yes, so the noun meaning fits. Does «Amir crashed into Sam» still make sense? Yes, so the verb meaning fits.
fact: A cannon is a big, heavy gun, usually on wheels or on a ship.
fact: A cannon fires large metal balls or shells.
fact: «Cannoned» means crashed into something hard while moving fast.
fact: «Water cannon» is a machine that sprays very strong jets of water.
fact: «Loose cannon» means a person nobody can control.
exercise: «The cannon they are shooting» in the Toad verse: what is a cannon? | A kind of bread | A small, soft toy | * A big, heavy gun that fires metal balls | A type of loud horn
exercise: «Amir cannoned into Sam in the corridor.» What does cannoned mean? | Waved happily at | * Crashed into, hard, while moving fast | Sprayed with water | Quietly walked past
exercise: What is a water cannon? | A bell that rings at school | * A machine that sprays very strong jets of water | A tall tower built for a castle
test: From the 1400s, «cannons began to smash even the thickest walls.» What could cannons do to castle walls? | Turn the walls into water | * Smash even the thickest walls | Make the walls soft and warm | Stop the walls from ever falling
test: Someone is called «a loose cannon». What does this mean? | * A person nobody can control | A person who is always silent | A person who fires guns at parties | A very old, heavy person
exam: In «The cannon was heavy and sat on wheels», what kind of word is cannon? | * A noun, a thing | A question word | A verb, an action | An adjective, a describing word
